<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nertobriga (Beturia)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nertobriga was an ancient town of the Celtici in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beturia">Beturia</a>, near Fregenal de la Sierra in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pliny-the-elder">Pliny the Elder</a> lists it among the Celtic towns of the region, and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> it bore the name Concordia Iulia. Its -briga ending marks a Celtic name; a Celtiberian town also called Nertobriga lay far away near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calatayud">Calatayud</a> in Aragon.</p></div>
